;; Go's AOT level's divergences from gc (bin/goi check --aot, REAP2; doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md
;; "As built: REAP2"), in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (RPS3): the classes every program of
;; the AOT check that does not pass falls into, each with why it is by design or deferred and
;; where that was decided (:pending: no decision yet, listed for the user). A program's class is
;; the first whose :match finds its result and reason ("RESULT REASON", as
;; test/goi/check-aot-linux-amd64.edn and test/goi/check-aot-known.edn write them). bin/goi
;; divergences --aot checks the reference against them (test/goi/divergences.ae). Where the cause
;; is one of goi's classes the id is goi's. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :positions
  :title "positions mode :lines does not keep: expressions' line breaks, //line directives"
  :kind :design
  :why "the run programs are printed from their forms of mode :lines in the lines layout (RPS17): each statement at its line, but a selector or call split over lines is printed on one, and the printed program has no //line directives, so a panic's or runtime.Caller's line is the statement's"
  :decided "RPS17 (a), SPEC.md §10.1"
  :match [#"^known positions: "]}
 {:id :toolchain
  :title "runs of the go command and the toolchain's root"
  :kind :design
  :why "the program runs the go command over $GOROOT/test (gc's run fails as the AOT program's, the log's times differ) or asks runtime.GOROOT, which go build -trimpath (arbace.build.go's) leaves empty"
  :decided "§1.1, GR4; BUILD.md (-trimpath)"
  :match [#"^known runs the go command" #"^known runtime\.GOROOT"]}
 {:id :go-build-complete
  :title "go build's -complete"
  :kind :design
  :why "arbace.build.go builds with go build, which compiles a package without assembly with -complete: a function without a body is an error there, where Go's test driver's rundir compiles without it and the test relies on gc eliminating the dead call"
  :decided :pending
  :match [#"^known go build's -complete: "]}
 {:id :no-forms
  :title "invalid programs without forms"
  :kind :design
  :why "an errorcheck program go/parser rejects or the converter cannot convert (GC47) has no final forms to print; goi judges it on gc's syntax errors or its raw forms, which the printer does not print"
  :decided "GC47, G1, GPS9, GPS43"
  :match [#"^unsupported no forms: an invalid program repr/go does not convert"]}
 {:id :printer-invalid
  :title "the printer refusing the forms of invalid programs"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the forms of mode :full of three invalid programs hold what the printer refuses (a spread outside a call's arguments, a method without a receiver, new and make without their type argument): the printer could print them as written"
  :decided :pending
  :match [#"^known errorcheck: the printer refuses the forms of an invalid program"]}
 {:id :spellings
  :title "the forms of invalid programs that say another program"
  :kind :design
  :why "goi's class GC49's kin at the AOT level: a function whose final statement is an expression is converted as returning it, so the program printed from its forms returns where the original does not and gc's \"missing return\" errors are not reported"
  :decided "GC49, SPEC.md §6.4"
  :match [#"^known errorcheck: the forms of an invalid program say another program"]}
 {:id :gc-reference
  :title "gc's own errors no longer pass the test"
  :kind :design
  :why "go1.27.1's gc fails the program's own // ERROR comments (its messages changed since the test was written): there is no reference to judge the AOT level against"
  :decided "GR7b"
  :match [#"^skip gc's own errorcheck does not pass here"]}
]
